 "text": "Hello, how are things going? The eye can sometimes trick you. Mixed a dark brown with a little yellow to match your skin undertone, rather than the white of the container. No, the yellow in the tube gives you the wrong answer. Hold the bottle in the sun and see what color the brown turns. Use a shadow patch test. Apply little brown to the bridge of your nose, where the skin is thin and you can see right away. Mixed for several days in a small container, or just a couple of swaps. Use it all, or it goes stale. The shadows under my eyes look dark.",
